== 3. Category Taxonomy Design ==

=== 3.1 Adaptive Hierarchical Structure ===

'''Wikipedia Pattern:''' 3-5 levels maximum depth

'''BITwiki Implementation:'''
```
Root Category: [Portal Name]
│
├── Core Concepts
│ ├── Fundamental Principles
│ ├── Key Theories
│ ├── Methods & Techniques
│ └── Applications
│
├── Domain Areas
│ ├── [Specific Domain 1]
│ ├── [Specific Domain 2]
│ └── [Additional Domains as needed]
│
├── Related Fields
│ ├── Adjacent Discipline 1
│ ├── Adjacent Discipline 2
│ └── [Dynamic expansion]
│
└── Resources
 ├── Organizations
 ├── Publications
 ├── People
 └── Tools & Software
```

=== 3.2 Category Naming Conventions ===

| Pattern | Example | Usage |
|---------|---------|-------|
| '''Field + Aspect''' | "Systems Science Concepts" | Core content categories |
| '''Aspect + Type''' | "Complexity Theories" | Thematic groupings |
| '''Domain + Application''' | "Network Analysis Methods" | Applied categories |
| '''Entity Type''' | "Systems Scientists" | People/organizations |
| '''Temporal + Domain''' | "History of Cybernetics" | Chronological categories |

=== 3.3 Cross-Category Linking ===

Each category should link to:
* Parent category (structural)
* Sibling categories (contextual)
* Related portal categories (semantic)

----
== 4. Interconnection Strategy ==

=== 4.1 Portal Link Architecture ===

| Portal Type | Link Approach | Diversity |
|-------------|--------------|-----------|
| Meta Hub | Rich multi-domain | Cross-cutting connections |
| Domain Portal | Domain-centric with bridges | Adjacent fields |
| Topical Portal | Thematic clustering | Related concepts |
| Functional Portal | Method-based | Applicable domains |
| Temporal Portal | Chronological | Period connections |
| Comparative Portal | Multi-perspective | Synthesis views |

=== 4.2 Link Categorization ===

```
Portal Links Include:
├── Parent Portal (structural hierarchy)
│ └── Meta-hub or domain parent
├── Sibling Portals (same level)
│ └── Related at same hierarchical level
├── Child Portals (specialization)
│ └── More specific sub-topics
├── Related Domains (semantic)
│ └── Adjacent fields and concepts
├── Cross-Cutting Themes (transversal)
│ └── Shared concepts across domains
└── External Resources (extension)
 └── Sister projects, external sites
```

=== 4.3 Relationship Indicators ===

| Symbol | Relationship | Example |
|--------|--------------|---------|
| ↑ | Parent portal | ↑ Systems Science |
| → | Sibling portal | → Mathematics |
| ↓ | Child portal | ↓ Network Theory |
| ↔ | Bidirectional | ↔ Complexity Science |
| ⇄ | Strong coupling | ⇄ Cybernetics |
| ⊕ | Cross-cutting | ⊕ Information Theory |

